{{also|mittel}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|mittel}}, from {{inh|de|goh|mittil}} (akin to {{cog|osx|middil}}), from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*midlą}}, {{m|gem-pro|*midilą}}, {{m|gem-pro|*medalą||middle}}, {{m|gem-pro|*midil-}}. Compare {{cog|nl|middel}}, {{cog|en|middle}}. See also {{m|de|Mitte}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈmɪtəl/|[ˈmɪtl̩]}}
* {{audio|de|De-Mittel.ogg|audio}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n}}

# [[agent]], [[appliance]]
# [[means]]
#* '''2010''', ''{{w|Der Spiegel}}'', issue [http://www.spiegel.de/spiegel/print/index-2010-31.html 31/2010], page 56:
#*: {{quote|de|Die Aufgabe eines Verteidigers besteht darin, für seine Mandanten mit allen '''Mitteln''' des Rechtsstaats zu kämpfen.|The duty of a defense lawyer consists of fighting for his clients with all constitutional means.}}
# [[medicament]], [[remedy]]
#: {{uxi|de|Ein [[ausgezeichnet|ausgezeichnetes]] [[Mittel]] gegen [[Arteriosklerose]].|An excellent '''remedy''' for arteriosclerosis.}}
# (only plural) [[funds]], [[capital]]
# [[median]]
# {{lb|de|uncountable|printing|dated}} The [[middle]] of the 7 [[traditional]] [[size]]s of [[German]] [[type]], between [[Cicero]] and [[Tertia]], [[standardize]]d as 14 [[point]] and [[taken]] as [[roughly]] [[equivalent]] to "[[English]]" [[type]].

